# R23 Wickermoor on the eve: the Round, the barricade, the bonfire, Dani, the retreat. By hand, polished by Gemini (R23 square), unvoiced.

~ arrive
Narrator: The Founder's Round is barricaded by folk with no practice at war: carts across the moor road, planks propped against wheels, a long supper table laid under the inn's lanterns. The village goat has taken the notice board.
set wv_square_seen
-> END

~ bonfire
Narrator: North of the rooftops, the fire on Rowan's Rise burns steady and high, sending a single grease-black pillar into the night. Folk in the Round have stared at it so long their eyes slide right past it.
set wv_bonfire_watched
-> END

~ barricade
Narrator: Hay-carts, loose boards, and a lifted garden fence choke the mouth of the north road. It might turn a curious calf.
* [Athletics DC 14] Put your shoulders to the carts and lock the axles -> barr_ok | barr_fail
* [Investigation DC 14] Spot the slack joints and wedge them tight -> barr_ok | barr_fail
* Set the militia to bracing it properly -> barr_ask
* Leave it as it stands -> END

~ barr_ok
Narrator: You heave the heavy timber into a true wall, leaving a narrow sally gap wide enough for a runner and shut to everything else.
set wv_barricade_built
temp_hp 2d8 party
-> END

~ barr_fail
Narrator: An iron-rimmed wheel slips its chock and kicks back against your shins. You have a fresh bruise, and the cart is where it started.
damage 1d6 bludgeoning
-> barricade

~ barr_ask
Narrator: The volunteers form a timber line and wedge the axles with cobblestones. It will win no prizes for joinery, but it holds.
set wv_barricade_built
-> END

~ dani
dani_jenkin [neutral]: They are all watching the fire, as if the fire had legs. It is the willow that walks. I saw its long strides in the well-water. Rest your boots while you may, we have not got an hour.
-> END

~ retreat_confirm
Narrator: Turning back leaves Rowan's Rise to the fire. The cult will burn every prisoner in the wicker cage, and the effigy will march down upon the village whole.
* Fall back to the Founder's Round and make our stand -> retreat_go
* Hold the hill and fight on -> END

~ retreat_go
Narrator: You turn your backs on the rise, and the ragged hymn behind you swells with a sudden, greedy joy.
set vigil_fled
set vigil_deaths += 6
quest wickers_vigil fallen_back
move wv_square:from_moors

~ fall_back_gate
Narrator: The carts hold, and a dry hush settles over the Round. Every face is turned toward the empty north road until the cobblestones begin to chatter in the dirt and the pole-lanterns swing.
Narrator: A giant of woven willow, taller than the church steeple, strides out of the moorland dark lit red by its own roaring ribs.
crooked_man [sly]: Nobody home upon the hill? How rude! Never mind, neighbour, I can step down to the parlour!
-> fall_back_menu

~ fall_back_menu
* Hold the Round against the effigy -> square_fight
* Flee down the south road and leave the village -> abandon

~ square_fight
Narrator: Its first sweeping fist takes the thatch and rafters off the nearest cottage.
combat wv_wicker_square

~ abandon
Narrator: You take the south road at a run. Behind you, the lanterns go dark one by one, and then the roofs begin to roar.
set wicker_man_triumphant
quest wickers_vigil ash_over_the_hollow
end_game
